note tests/a64efi/om2.om: `target a64efi` then `om2` (the lines run.sh puts first, with efirt.om).
note An OM-2 form (an unsized array parameter) and globals read and written, with no pinned register:
note the program prints ==B, om2 7 26, ==E through efi 13.
global obuf uchar 32
global acc ulong 4

fn sum a view uchar * n ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong n
s = add s ulong get a i
end
ret s
end

fn main to ulong
t = new uchar 4 0
put t 0 5
put t 1 6
put t 2 7
put t 3 8
put acc 1 7
put acc 2 sum t 4
put obuf 0 61
put obuf 1 61
put obuf 2 66
put obuf 3 10
put obuf 4 111
put obuf 5 109
put obuf 6 50
put obuf 7 32
put obuf 8 uchar add 48 get acc 1
put obuf 9 32
put obuf 10 uchar add 48 div get acc 2 10
put obuf 11 uchar add 48 rem get acc 2 10
put obuf 12 10
put obuf 13 61
put obuf 14 61
put obuf 15 69
put obuf 16 10
r = efi 13 0 obuf 0 17
ret 0
end
